### Snapshot #11, reviewer "Review · Grok medium", grok grok-4.7: done

PDF uploads no longer post a client-made JPEG preview. After each page upload or reuse write, `pdfthumbnails` polls `GET /api/queues` until thumbnails, search indexing, in-memory search processing, and pending writes are all empty (five minutes, then the run stops; a 429 is not retried). The server adds those queue counts, including a new search-processing flag, and the tool copies the first page's server thumbnail onto the PDF and onto reused page rows.

- The thumbnail queue stays pending after the thumbnailer gives up, so `pdfthumbnails` hits its five-minute limit and uploads nothing.
- An in-memory search rebuild can publish a stale index and still report search processing idle, so the uploader sends the next page while that rebuild is outstanding.

### Snapshot #12, reviewer "Review · Grok medium", grok grok-4.7: done

PDF page uploads now wait until server thumbnails, search indexing, the in-memory search rebuild, and pending writes have all drained, and a 429 or a queue that stays busy for five minutes stops the run. The client no longer posts a preview JPEG: the server thumbnails each uploaded page, and the client copies the first page's thumbnail onto the PDF. Reused pages copy that thumbnail and its completion stamp as well, so they do not re-enter the thumbnail worker. Failed thumbnail attempts are counted in process memory; after three failures the document drops out of the pending count until the process restarts. Super-admin bearer tokens can read GET /api/queues, which is what the uploader polls.

- `TestSharedPDFUploadsOnceAndReusesCompletedPages` still expects a PDF download for a rendered file whose page thumbnail only needs to be copied, so the missing-thumbnail cases fail.

### Snapshot #13, reviewer "Review · Grok low", grok grok-4.7: done

PDF thumbnail uploads now wait until the server has drained thumbnail generation, search indexing, in-memory search processing, and pending writes before the next page or reuse write, and they stop on a 429 or if that drain takes more than five minutes. The client no longer uploads its own preview JPEG. After the server thumbnails the first page image, the tool copies that thumbnail onto the PDF, and reused pages copy both the image and the thumbnail. Queue reporting shares the thumbnailer's attempt counts and adds a search-processing gauge. Search index rebuilds skip a publish when a follow pass does not change rows, so thumbnail-only writes do not rebuild the in-memory index.

